// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 09-identity-origin-extent
// facility: rule.ref.form [Ref-Form-Not-Place] (D-0084 admits operator results and literals only as call arguments); conf.temp-borrow-literal-binding-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.borrow-of-non-place (static)
//
// Outside a call's argument list, a literal (or an operator's result) is
// not a place and is not borrowed: it would end with the statement, and
// the reference with it. Bind it first.

import std;

fn main()
{
    ref<i32, shared> r = &5;
    printf("%d\n", *r);
}
